  "world": {
   "notes": "This is the Heart Attack Grill in downtown Las Vegas: a hospital-themed burger restaurant where customers are \"patients\" in gowns, orders are \"prescriptions\", waitresses dress as nurses, and diners who don't finish are spanked. Anyone over 350 pounds eats free after a public weigh-in. It's cash only. The Quadruple Bypass Burger was once certified by Guinness as the world's most calorific burger. Menu prices are as recently listed. The Grill was founded in Arizona in 2005 and moved to Fremont Street in 2011. Two of its larger-than-life spokesmen died in 2011 and 2013, and the press still brings it up whenever something happens. In the real world the Grill closed in May 2026 when its lease ran out; this save starts earlier, while it's still open. Sales, seat count and rent are estimates. Staff names are invented, and the player is not the real founder. Keep this a business simulation, not a lecture: characters can criticise the concept, but the owner decides.",
